@startuml
title Evidence and signal relationships - target conceptual model
class "Original input / selected evidence" as Evidence
class Measurement
class Signal
class "Optional normalised value" as Normalised
class "Derived signal" as Derived
class "Diagnostic insight" as DiagnosticInsight
class "Evidence relationship" as Relationship
class "Intelligence evaluation" as Evaluation
class Provenance
Evidence --> Measurement : may inform
Evidence --> Signal : may inform
Evidence --> Relationship : may directly inform
Measurement --> Signal : may inform
Signal --> Normalised : optional
Signal --> Derived : may inform
Evidence --> DiagnosticInsight
Signal --> DiagnosticInsight
Derived --> DiagnosticInsight
DiagnosticInsight --> Relationship
Relationship --> Evaluation
Provenance .. Evidence
Provenance .. Measurement
Provenance .. Signal
Provenance .. Derived
Provenance .. Relationship
note bottom of Relationship
  Support, challenge, context, missing,
  not evaluated, or related but insufficiently relevant.
  Shared sources are not independent corroboration.
end note
note bottom of Evaluation
  Reliability, evidence strength and confidence differ.
  Confidence and priority are dynamic and distinct.
end note
@enduml
